y Trump is mostly to blame for the  shutdown 35% say Democrats for  percent say Republicans next question do  voters see the shutdown in and of itself  as a problem in other words is the  shutdown aside from the goals of the  shutdown as stated by Trump is the  shutdown itself a problem 46% of  registered voters say that it is a  crisis that the government shutdown is a  crisis 35% believe that the government  shutdown is a problem meaning that in  total eighty-one percent of registered  voters believe the shutdown in and of  itself is a crisis or problem and not  good numbers for Donald Trump and then  lastly what about the wall the question  if the only way to end the government  shutdown is to dedicate funds for a  border wall along the United  states-mexico border would you support  or oppose it 3% would strongly support  border wall funding if it were the only  way to end the shutdown and remember  it's not the only way to end the  shutdown Trump is claiming that's the  only way he will be willing to end the  shutdown but it's not this is a  hypothetical only 3% would strongly  support funding the border wall if it  were the only way to end the shutdown 4%  would somewhat somewhat support funding  the border wall if it were the only way  to end the shutdown so in total only 7%  of Americans either somewhat or strongly  support a government shutdown if it's  the only way to ultimately get to border  wall funding  13% somewhat opposed it 59% strongly  oppose it my thought on this Pat is that  that 7% must be really really active on  Twitter because they are an  extraordinarily loud 7% yeah most of  these numbers make sense to me the fact  though that 46% of Americans identified  the shutdown of the crisis and 35  percent identified as a problem that  totals 81 percent and yet we still have  40 percent of Americans approving of the  President how does that square up  I thought his base of support was a  little bit lower than 40 percent I  thought it was maybe 30 3